From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Chrome lives on when the Linux session's D-Bus goes

Chrome talks to the Linux session's D-Bus (nickel-session's, at
/run/user/<uid>/bus) for KDE Connect (0028) and cloud storage (0050), on
private connections. That bus ends when the session does, at sign-out,
before Chrome has exited; and dbus::Bus aborts the whole process when any
of its connections is lost ("D-Bus connection was disconnected.
Aborting."), as it should for the system's buses. So every sign-out
crashed Chrome: a crash report each time, and at the next sign-in
"Chromium didn't shut down correctly" with a browser window it reopened.

The KDE Connect and cloud storage connections give dbus::Bus a
disconnected_callback (Chrome 157: "dbus: Let desktop Linux end the
session instead of crashing when a bus is lost"): a lost connection is
logged and its calls fail from then on. Up to Chrome 156 this patch added
its own Options::abort_on_disconnect to dbus::Bus.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/file_manager/nickel_cloud_client.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/file_manager/nickel_cloud_client.cc
index bb3437af40e78..4b9bf621fcf3c 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/file_manager/nickel_cloud_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/file_manager/nickel_cloud_client.cc
@@ -78,6 +78,10 @@ void NickelCloudClient::Connect() {
   options.address = base::StringPrintf("unix:path=/run/user/%u/bus",
                                        static_cast<unsigned>(getuid()));
   options.connection_type = dbus::Bus::PRIVATE;
+  // It ends at sign-out, before Chrome does: logged, and its calls fail
+  // from then on (without a callback, dbus::Bus aborts Chrome).
+  options.disconnected_callback = base::BindOnce(
+      [] { LOG(WARNING) << "the Linux session's D-Bus is gone"; });
   options.dbus_task_runner = DBusThread()->task_runner();
   bus_ = base::MakeRefCounted<dbus::Bus>(std::move(options));
   bus_->GetDBusTaskRunner()->PostTaskAndReplyWithResult(
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/ash/settings/pages/multidevice/nickel_phones_handler.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/ash/settings/pages/multidevice/nickel_phones_handler.cc
index bd4284bc62836..fff60459cbe08 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/webui/ash/settings/pages/multidevice/nickel_phones_handler.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/webui/ash/settings/pages/multidevice/nickel_phones_handler.cc
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include "base/containers/fixed_flat_set.h"
 #include "base/files/file_path.h"
 #include "base/functional/bind.h"
+#include "base/logging.h"
 #include "base/message_loop/message_pump_type.h"
 #include "base/no_destructor.h"
 #include "base/strings/stringprintf.h"
@@ -68,6 +69,10 @@ dbus::Bus* SessionBus() {
     options.address = base::StringPrintf("unix:path=/run/user/%u/bus",
                                          static_cast<unsigned>(getuid()));
     options.connection_type = dbus::Bus::PRIVATE;
+    // It ends at sign-out, before Chrome does: logged, and its calls fail
+    // from then on (without a callback, dbus::Bus aborts Chrome).
+    options.disconnected_callback = base::BindOnce(
+        [] { LOG(WARNING) << "the Linux session's D-Bus is gone"; });
     options.dbus_task_runner = thread->task_runner();
     *bus = base::MakeRefCounted<dbus::Bus>(std::move(options));
   }
